# Buckeye train -- 24 speakers (60.0%), 13473 utterances (60.0%).
# Buckeye ships NO official split; this is a FA-Bench convention.
# 60/20/20 by SPEAKER, stratified on the corpus's own design axes
# (sex x age -- see datasets/en/buckeye/speakers.tsv, corpus manual
# Table 1). 60/20/20 divides the 4x10 design exactly: every cell
# gives 6 train / 2 dev / 2 test, so the splits are balanced at the
# CELL level, not merely on the marginals. Within each cell the two
# speakers are chosen so the split also approximates 20% of that
# cell's utterances. Deterministic, no seed.
# balance: sex f/m 12/12   age y/o 12/12   cells fy/fo/my/mo 6/6/6/6
# speakers: s01,s02,s03,s06,s09,s11,s12,s13,s15,s16,s17,s18,s19,s20,s21,s24,s26,s27,s29,s30,s33,s36,s38,s39
